+### A11/A12 — adjacent growth bounds (`SoringP1/StrictMonotone.lean`, `Lipschitz.lean`)
+- `S_strict_mono {n} (hn : 1 ≤ n) : S n + 1 ≤ S (n + 1)` — strict growth at
+  every positive input. The proof removes the last key from an optimal
+  `(n+1)`-key tree, measures execution length on reachable rankings (rather
+  than syntactic height), and trims unreachable branches before applying
+  minimality.
+- `S_lipschitz (n) : S (n + 1) ≤ S n + Nat.clog 2 (n + 1)` — valid for all
+  `n`, including `n=0`. Lift an optimal tree on the first `n` labels; at each
+  leaf, binary-search the last label's insertion rank in the sorted output.
+  The search has height at most `ceil(log₂(n+1))` and the resulting tree sorts
+  every ranking. The helper `rel` re-ranks the first `n` labels by their
+  restriction from a full ranking; no cost or complexity-class claim is made.
+
